{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y_obs`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only observed data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level data variable `y_obs`, which is observed exactly once with the built-in `poisson_log` distribution. The parameter `f_tilde` is given exactly one built-in prior before its transformed-parameter-dependent value `f_predict` is used in the likelihood. Other data variables are context inputs used only for dimensions, indexing, and covariance construction.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N_predict;
  array[N_predict] real x_predict;

  int<lower=1> N_obs;
  array[N_obs] int y_obs;
  array[N_obs] int<lower=1, upper=N_predict> observed_idx;

  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N_predict, N_predict] cov =   gp_exp_quad_cov(x_predict, alpha, rho)
                                     + diag_matrix(rep_vector(1e-10, N_predict));
  matrix[N_predict, N_predict] L_cov = cholesky_decompose(cov);
}

parameters {
  vector[N_predict] f_tilde;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[N_predict] f_predict = L_cov * f_tilde;
}

model {
  f_tilde ~ normal(0, 1);
  y_obs ~ poisson_log(f_predict[observed_idx]);
}

generated quantities {
  array[N_predict] int y_predict = poisson_log_rng(f_predict);
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "N_obs": 1,
  "N_predict": 3,
  "alpha": 4.95377431668197,
  "observed_idx": [
    2
  ],
  "rho": 0.5284448743787199,
  "x_predict": [
    1.0,
    2.0,
    3.0
  ],
  "y_obs": [
    1
  ]
}","protected_variables":["y_obs"]}
